Each verdict compares the author's result and derivation with FIRST, then considers retained conditions, admissible zeros and the requested extraction/inward-factor form. Domain conditions may be supplied by the author's `domain`, result or derivation. A separately enumerated zero is not required when the stated nonstrict domain and matching expression already retain it. Optional intrinsic domains outside explicit source conditions are not required.

Decimal versus fractional coefficients, multiplication placement and plain-text versus LaTeX cases are accepted notation differences where the frozen forms already establish the same expression. No new arithmetic samples or mathematical validation were added.

